   "landed 2026-07-09: kotoba-lang/standard-model#1 merged as
    315ec62e88f77aa02d62e3d05d90e08edcac1997, 30 tests/428 assertions
    (up from 22/85 at ADR-2607051500), CI green JDK 17+21"
   "PR #1's own honesty tests surfaced a real bug: kotoba.sm.gauge/structure-constants's
    formula f^abc=-2i Tr([T^a,T^b]T^c) hard-codes Tr(T^aT^b)=1/2delta^ab, true for
    the compact SU(2)/SU(3) generators it was built against but false for so(1,3)'s
    noncompact bivector generators (diagonal trace-Gram matrix but +/-1, not a
    uniform +1/2 -- boost-type generators -1, rotation-type +1). Applied as-is this
    silently returned values 2x too large and wrong-signed for boost-type third
    indices, verified for all 216 structure-constant triples"
   "kotoba-lang/standard-model#2 (in review 2026-07-09, CI green JDK 17+21,
    33 tests/1114 assertions) generalizes structure-constants to
    f^ABD = -i Tr([T_A,T_B]T_D) / K^DD using the generator set's OWN trace-Gram
    matrix K^AB=Tr(T_A T_B), computed via new generator-gram/diagonal-gram-real;
    scope limited to diagonal K (enforced at runtime via ex-info, non-diagonal
    generalization deliberately deferred); proven backward-compatible for
    SU(2)/SU(3) (K^DD=1/2 uniformly reduces the new formula exactly to the old
    -2i one, verified element-wise against an independent reimplementation of
    the legacy formula, not just textbook values); so(1,3) raw and independently-
    derived true structure constants now agree exactly (max |raw-true|=0.0 over
    216 triples)"
   "explicitly OUT OF SCOPE, not implemented in either PR: position gauge field
    h_mu, derived metric g_munu=h_mu.h_nu, Riemann/Ricci curvature scalars,
    Einstein multivector, the GTG action principle and field equations, any
    proof of GR-equivalence (cited as an established 1998 literature result, not
    re-derived), de Sitter/Cl(1,4) extensions, MacDowell-Mansouri constructions,
    and any dark-matter/dark-energy/entropy sector"
   "context: this follows a pre-implementation co-scientist-style Workflow run
